      "report": "# GATHER: integration test, pass 1\n\nThree full checks ran, each with `awwo-check-page gather.html --out <dir> --viewport 960x600 --wait-ms 3000 --timeout-ms 40000 --budget-ms 115000 --frames 1,5,9,14,20 --expect-motion --max-draw-calls 120 --max-triangles 400000`. The page delivered is the one check 3 ran on.\n\n## First check (original page)\n- Verdict: **fail**, exit 1. \"The page did not load within 10000 ms\"; the screenshot timed out (5000 ms).\n- Tests: the self-test did not run (0 passed of 0 reported, out of the 27 expected).\n- Plants caught: 0 of 0 reported (9 expected).\n- Page errors: 0.\n- Blank: not measured (no screenshot).\n- Frames taken: 0 (\"the page did not load\"). Most draw calls / triangles in a frame: 0 / 0. Still or moving: not measured.\n\n## Last check (check 3)\n- Verdict: **error**, exit 3. \"The check ran out of its 115000 ms budget.\" Timings: load 2880 ms, wait 3000 ms, screenshot 6798 ms, self-test 21796 ms, total 116073 ms.\n- Tests: **27 / 27 passed**.\n- Plants caught: **9 / 9**.\n- Page errors: 0.\n- Blank: not reported (the blank flag and pixels are null; no screenshot file was recorded).\n- Frames taken: **0**. The budget ran out before the frames stage, so the report gives no mode and no reason. Most draw calls / triangles in a frame: 0 / 0 (none measured). Still or moving: not measured.\n- Held clock: it ran and found renderAt; no failure, no note and no unfinished step.\n\n(Check 2, after fix 1: 27 / 27 tests, 9 / 9 plants, 0 page errors. The screenshot timed out at 20000 ms, the budget ran out at 116063 ms and 0 frames were taken.)\n\n## Fixes (one line each)\n1. render: the default-size RoomEnvironment PMREM (`pm.fromScene(room, 0.04)`) left about 10 s of GPU work that stalled the first render in the headless browser, so the page never fired `load`. Changed to `pm.fromScene(room, 0.04, 0.1, 100, { size: 64 })`. After this the page loaded in about 2.9 s and the self-test ran.\n2. render: with `antialias: true`, the first screenshot took 14.9 to 20 s. Changed to `antialias: false`. In check 3 the screenshot took 6.8 s and the self-test 21.8 s, but the whole check still ran past its 115 s budget.\n\n## Failing tests\n- None in checks 2 and 3. In check 1 no test ran because the page never loaded.\n\n## Still wrong\n- **The frames have not been taken, so the page has not been shown to render frame by frame at 1, 5, 9, 14 and 20 s.** Draw calls, triangles, blankness and motion per frame are all unverified. The checks run out of their 115 s budget after the screenshot and the self-test.\n- What timing probes found (instrumented copies in dbg/, not delivered): after the fixes, normal frames take 1 to 80 ms, but the first frame of a fresh load still costs about 1.9 s for shader and texture setup. The first screenshot is slow in this software GL. A third copy of the self-test's run is not the cost: the self-test itself takes 22 to 34 s.\n- I did not find where the remaining ~85 s of the budget goes. The report has no timing for the stages after the self-test. A next step for pass 2: run the check with only `--frames`, or with a larger `--budget-ms` if the command limit allows, to see whether the frames stage itself is slow (each renderAt replays from 0 at 60 steps per second, which is up to 1,200 glass steps).\n- The screenshot was not inspected, because none was saved in checks 2 and 3. Nothing visual is claimed.\n",
