      "output": "**Static review:** I ran nothing. This comes only from the two reports; anything they don't show is **not actually run**.\n\n**Tests after pass 2 (exit 0):** 27 of 27 passed, none failed. The reports give only the total, not each test's result. By owner: core 1–3, render 4–6, glass 7–14, look 15–17, bench 18–19, hands 20–22, sound 23–24, panel 25–27.\n\n**Planted failures:** all 9 (P1–P9) caught. The reports don't say which test caught each.\n\n**Frames:** all 5 taken (1, 5, 9, 14, 20 s).\n- Most in a frame: 51 draw calls and 18,530 triangles, against 120 and 400,000.\n- They move; none is still.\n- None is blank: the screenshot had 179 colours.\n\n**What pass 2 says the frames show:** judged **from their numbers only**; it never saw them (no image tool). Each reading is a guess.\n- 1 s: lit, 1.2 % bright, read as a hot gather.\n- 5 s: brightest, read as reheat and blow.\n- 9 s: biggest change (59 %), read as swing and jacks.\n- 14 s: smallest change (9.6 %).\n- 20 s: darkest, read as cooled glass.\n\n**What the fixes changed:**\n- **Pass 1:** the room lighting map was cut to 64 px, so the page loads, and antialiasing was turned off. Tests passed, but checks still ran out of time and no frames were taken.\n- **Pass 2:**\n  - Software renderers start on the low quality tier.\n  - During the self-test, redraws are skipped when nothing changed. This applies only to testing, so tests 4–6 draw less often.\n  - After a draw over 60 ms, the loop waits three times as long.\n\n**Not covered by any test or frame (not actually run):**\n- How the glass looks: refraction, tint, glow colour, bloom, dust, turning.\n- The vessel's shape on screen at 20 s.\n- The script after 20 s: knock-off, colour change, shelf.\n- Slumping and the grades.\n- Phone framing, camera drift, orbit, zoom.\n- Quarter speed, Show rings, the rpm display.\n- The page's text, and whether panels overlap.\n- A real GPU.\n- Sound beyond the offline tests.",
